# Per-site New Relic credentials for nr-pull.sh.
#
# NEVER put a filled-in nr.env inside vendor/augustash/claude-config — this package ships
# to every project, so a real key here would propagate to all of them. That is the only
# hard rule; the site repo itself is fine, and is the better home.
#
# PREFERRED — a gitignored dir in the site, next to the site it belongs to:
#   mkdir -p .newrelic && cp <this file> .newrelic/nr.env && chmod 600 .newrelic/nr.env
#   echo '/.newrelic/' >> .gitignore
#   git check-ignore -v .newrelic/nr.env        # verify before writing the key
#
# A directory, not a bare file: nr-pull.sh writes <site-dir>/out/ and nr-report.py writes
# report.html + CSVs into it, and none of that should be committed. One rule covers all.
#
# Keep it in the site because a parallel ~/.config tree is a place nobody looks — a
# credential filed there goes missing the moment you stop thinking about it.
#
# FALLBACK — ~/.config/newrelic/<site>/nr.env, when the repo is not yours to add an ignore
# rule to, when the deploy artifact would sweep the file in regardless, or when
# git check-ignore does not confirm the rule.
#
# NR_ACCOUNT_ID  : the number in your New Relic URL (.../accounts/<ID>/...) or on the API keys page
# NR_API_KEY     : a New Relic "User" key (starts with NRAK-), created at New Relic > user menu > API keys
# NR_APP         : APM app name; Pantheon names it "<site> (<env>)" e.g. "mspairport (live)".
#                  QUOTE IT -- the parentheses are shell syntax and break sourcing otherwise.
#                  Confirm it from the site rather than guessing:
#                    terminus drush <site>.<env> -- php-eval 'echo ini_get("newrelic.appname");'
# NR_TXN_FILTER  : optional extra NRQL predicate to narrow the percentile query to some
#                  subset of traffic. Leave unset for site-wide.
# NR_ENDPOINT    : optional; defaults to US. EU accounts: https://api.eu.newrelic.com/graphql

NR_ACCOUNT_ID=
NR_API_KEY=NRAK-
NR_APP=""
# NR_TXN_FILTER=
# NR_ENDPOINT=https://api.newrelic.com/graphql
